eport use this file's `energy_density_wh_kg` 195	- **Errors**: `bda error: ...` + exit code 1 — missing parameter keys (`KeyError`), `--sim` not valid JSON, numeric type mismatch; first check `--sim` points to a 1C discharge output and `--base` has the corresponding keys 196	 197	## run-tr — thermal-runaway three-side-reaction ODE (Stage 4 abuse scenarios) 198	 199	``` 200	bda run-tr [--sim S] [--mass-kg M] [--t-init T] [--x0 X] [--t-max T] [--mcp M] [--hA H] [--t-amb T] [--q-nail W] --out OUT 201	``` 202	 203	- **Model**: zero-dimensional lumped thermal balance + three-side-reaction Arrhenius kinetics (SEI decomposition / negative-electrolyte / positive-electrolyte), scipy BDF stiff integration; first-order reactant consumption guarantees energy conservation (bounded T_max) 204	- **Trigger judgment (mechanical)**: dT/dt > 1 K/s (temperature-rise inflection) or T ≥ 573 K (300°C red line) → `triggered: true` + `trigger_time_s` 205	- **Overcharge → thermal runaway auto-coupling**: `--sim` passes run-pyamm output (e.g., overcharge protocol), auto-reads its `T_max_K` as initial temperature 206	- **Nail**: `--q-nail` short-circuit heat source (W) 207	- **Output keys**: `triggered`, `trigger_time_s`, `T_max_K`, `T_final_K`, `dTdt_max_K_s`, `T_series_K`, `t_series_s`, `params` 208	- **--mass-kg mandatory**: pass the cell mass from calc-energy's `mass_kg` → mcp = mass×900; otherwise mcp fixed at 1000 systematically distorts small cells (t7_r1 incident: a 40 g cell was judged as 1 kg) 209	- **Errors**: `--sim` file missing `T_max_K` key → should pass a run-pyamm output JSON 210	 211	## run-cp2k — molecular true DFT cross-validation (only closing Top-3, optional) 212	 213	``` 214	bda run-cp2k --in IN --out OUT 215	``` 216	 217	- **Isomorphic output with run-orca** (same batch of molecules under two independent programs, removing program-implementation-difference concerns): `{"candidates": [{"smiles": ..., "endorsement": {E_hartree, homo_ev, lumo_ev, ie_ev, ea_ev, converged}}]}` — `ie_ev`/`ea_ev` are **vertical** single points of cation/anion states on the neutral optimized geometry (consistent with run-orca) 218	- **Method**: PBE + D3(BJ) dispersion correction, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH short-range basis + GTH-PBE pseudopotentials (H/C/O/F/N/S/P/B/Li), 20 Å vacuum box for isolated molecules (PERIODIC NONE + Poisson MT); neutral state GEO_OPT, ionic states ENERGY single points 219	- **Environment**: MSYS2 `pacman -S mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-cp2k`; data files `C:\cp2k-data` (BASIS_MOLOPT/GTH_POTENTIALS/dftd3.dat, downloaded from the cp2k/cp2k GitHub data/ directory; override with env var `CP2K_DATA_DIR`) 220	- **Two known pitfalls (runner auto-handles)**: ① MSYS2 stock cp2k.ssmp.exe reserves 2 MB stack — large molecules overflow at initialization — runner auto-prefers the pefile-patched `cp2k_stack4g.exe`; ② DBCSR reads `/proc/self/statm` at SCF start (no Windows CRTL path translation) — runner places a static page-count file at `C:\proc\self\statm`, runs via MSYS2 bash, caps OMP_NUM_THREADS at 8 (32 threads easily exhaust memory and crash), OMP_STACKSIZE 512M 221	- **Cost**: CPU minutes per small molecule (FEC-class 10 atoms ≈ 15–40 min/molecule) — **closing Top-3 only, forbidden inside the funnel** (same iron rule as run-orca; skipped when `real_compute: false`) 222	- **Errors**: 223	  - `cp2k not found; install: ...` → install the MSYS2 cp2k package per guidance 224	  - `CP2K data dir not found; ...` → download data files to `C:\cp2k-data` or set CP2K_DATA_DIR 225	  - `invalid SMILES: ...` / `failed to embed 3D structure ...` → RDKit cannot parse/generate conformer; check SMILES 226	  - `cp2k produced no total energy` → read *.out in the work directory (SCF non-convergence common: loosen EPS_SCF tolerance or increase MAX_SCF) 227	  - Single-candidate failure does not break the whole batch: that candidate outputs `{"smiles": ..., "error": "..."}`, the rest return normally 228
