XXV<0 derived)` — consistent with manual judgment 160	- **verdict rules**: threshold forms `{"min": n}` (greater-or-equal) / `{"max": n}` / boolean equality / scalar (treated as min); all checked metrics pass → `pass`, else `fail`; output missing a criteria metric → record `unchecked` and append "unchecked criteria: ..." to note (legitimate gap when stage not yet reached; verdict judged on checked metrics) 161	- **Output entry**: `{"action": "evaluate", "round": N, "metrics": {...scalars}, "verdict": "pass"|"fail", "evidence": [{"metric", "value", "threshold", "verdict", "source": "file:key"}, ...], "candidate"?, "unchecked"?, "note"?}` — evidence source is case-relative path (audit log replayable across machines) 162	- **Multiple candidates in same round**: one entry per evaluated candidate (multiple calls same round, distinguished by `--candidate`); report merges display by round 163	- Errors: 164	  - `entry-0 criteria not found in log.jsonl` → write criteria before evaluating 165	  - `output file does not exist: ...` → check path (relative to case-dir's cell/ directory) 166	  - `no criteria metrics in output files` → output keys entirely mismatch criteria; check whether the wrong file was passed 167	  - threshold dict has bound but value non-numeric → fail (non-judgable forms always fail — rather fail than fake pass) 168	 169	## verify-deliverables — deliverable protocol-compliance check 170	 171	``` 172	bda verify-deliverables --case-dir D 173	``` 174	 175	- **Check items (all mechanical)**: ① 7 deliverable categories complete (design_spec/bom/datasheet/calc/dvpr/dfmea/delivery_index, each with source file + PDF release) ② PDF non-empty (>1KB) ③ xlsx parseable with no empty sheets ④ delivery_index contains a VBF numbering list (≥5) ⑤ **audit chain complete: every propose round must have a same-round evaluate entry** (log-evaluate protocol prerequisite — evaluation without log entries leaves report conclusions without audit backing) 176	- **Output**: per-item `[PASS]/[FAIL]` + summary `ALL PASS`/`HAS FAILURES`; exit code 0/1 177	- **Error handling**: FAIL = protocol unmet; fix per detail and rerun (e.g., "propose round without evaluation: R01" → add log-evaluate entries); `missing log.jsonl` → protocol execution must have logs 178	 179	## calc-energy — contract-caliber energy density (same formula for all tasks) 180	 181	``` 182	bda calc-energy --sim S [--params P] [--base B] --out O 183	``` 184	 185	- **Formula (contract caliber, preventing cross-task precedent copying)**: `ED = ∫V·I_1C dt / Σ(layer thickness×(1−porosity)×density×area)` 186	  - Discharge energy = trapezoidal integral of `voltage_v`×`time_s` × I_1C, ÷3600 for Wh; I_1C = `Nominal cell capacity [A.h]` × 1 (constant current) 187	  - Area = `Electrode height [m]` × `Electrode width [m]` 188	  - Layers: positive/negative active layers (porosity factor applied), positive/negative current collectors (no porosity factor), separator — all from the parameter set used by `--base` (default Chen2020) or overridden by `--params` 189	  - **Electrolyte excluded from mass** (parameter set lacks density) — output `electrolyte_included: false` annotated honestly 190	- **Input**: `--sim` = discharge simulation output JSON (must contain `voltage_v` list, `time_s` list, `capacity_ah` scalar); `--params` optional, overrides the parameter set (the same params file used by run-pyamm) 191	- **Output**: `{capacity_ah, energy_wh, mass_kg, energy_density_wh_kg, volume_m3, energy_density_wh_l, thickness_m, midpoint_voltage_v, dcr_ohm, power_density_w_kg, layer_kg_m2 (per layer kg/m²), area_m2, electrolyte_included: false, note}` 192	  - `energy_density_wh_l` = energy/volume (volume = Σ layer thickness×area; contract caliber excludes electrolyte/casing) 193	  - `midpoint_voltage_v` = voltage at discharge-time midpoint (plateau-voltage approximation); `dcr_ohm` = DC resistance (start OCV − voltage at 10% discharge ÷ I_1C); `power_density_w_kg` = V_OC²/(4·DCR) ÷ mass 194	  - Judgment and report use this file's `energy_density_wh_kg` 195	- **Errors**: `bda error: ...` + exit code 1 — missing parameter keys (`KeyError`), `--sim` not valid JSON, numeric type mismatch; first check `--sim` points to a 1C discharge output and `--base` has the corresponding keys 196	 197	## run-tr — thermal-runaway three-side-reaction ODE (Stage 4 abuse scenarios) 198	 199	``` 200	bda run-tr [--sim S] [--mass-kg M] [--t-init T] [--x0 X] [--t-max T] [--mcp M] [--hA H] [--t-amb T] [--q-nail W] --out OUT 201	``` 202	 203	- **Model**: zero-dimensional lumped thermal balance + three-side-reaction Arrhenius kinetics (SEI decomposition / negative-electrolyte / positive-electrolyte), scipy BDF stiff integration; first-order reactant consumption guarantees energy conservation (bounded T_max) 204	- **Trigger judgment (mechanical)**: dT/dt > 1 K/s (temperature-rise inflection) or T ≥ 573 K (300°C red line) → `triggered: true` + `trigger_time_s` 205	- **Overcharge → thermal runaway auto-coupling**: `--sim` passes run-pyamm output (e.g., overcharge protocol), auto-reads its `T_max_K` as initial temperature 206	- **Nail**: `--q-nail` short-circuit heat source (W) 207	- **Output keys**: `triggered`, `trigger_time_s`, `T_max_K`, `T_final_K`, `dTdt_max_K_s`, `T_series_K`, `t_series_s`, `params` 208	- **--mass-kg mandatory**: pass the cell mass from calc-energy's `mass_kg` → mcp = mass×900; otherwise mcp fixed at 1000 systematically distorts small cells (t7_r1 incident: a 40 g cell was judged as 1 kg) 209	- **Errors**: `--sim` file missing `T_max_K` key → should pass a run-pyamm output JSON 210	 211	## run-cp2k — molecular true DFT cross-validation (only closing Top-3, optional) 212	 213	``` 214	bda run-cp2k --in IN --out OUT 215	``` 216	 217	- **Isomorphic output with run-orca** (same batch of molecules under two independent programs, removing program-implementation-difference concerns): `{"candidates": [{"smiles": ..., "endorsement": {E_hartree, homo_ev, lumo_ev, ie_ev, ea_ev, converged}}]